{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED. Required: (1) Correct the delivery claim and cursor contract. OTLP acceptance and durable cursor advancement are separate commits, so a crash after HTTP 200 and before cursor persistence re-emits even without rewrite; rotation, truncation, compaction, cursor loss, or source deletion add further duplicate/loss cases. Specify at-least-once delivery, a stable source-entry identity exposed to folds, cursor advancement only after durable acceptance, partial-line handling, and the limits under which backpressure can truthfully avoid loss. (2) Reconcile the product/privacy contradiction: zero-configuration history and disk-first default conflict with explicit per-harness opt-in. Disk ingestion must be disabled until explicit enablement, with selected roots and a plain sensitive-content warning. Paired repository fixtures must be synthetic or irreversibly scrubbed; real local transcripts and tool results must not be committed, and real-history size research should retain aggregate measurements only. Soften complete and strictly-more claims because stores can compact/delete and OTLP uniquely carries metrics/spans. (3) Define the OTLP mapping boundary precisely. Current canonical event.source is derived first from service.name and shipped bundles treat it as the harness; service.name=tailapp-reader would therefore hide claude_code/codex unless a declared harness attribute and normalizer rule are added. Specify stable service/source, harness, event-name, original timestamp, backfill marker, source-generation/entry identity, and chunk/truncation metadata. Splitting must be deterministic and distinguishable from independent events; truncation must be explicit. (4) Extend the research matrix to exercise crash-after-ACK-before-checkpoint, partial final lines, append during read, truncate-in-place, rename/replace, compaction, archived sessions, malformed/oversize entries, and source disappearance while backpressured; the present path+inode+offset sketch does not settle these cases. Advisories: the sidecar/OTLP boundary is architecturally sound and namespace-by-default is the right initial overlap policy; keep fusion conditional on paired identity evidence. Pin the exact CodeBurn revision surveyed (its current MIT-licensed provider docs show active format/discovery evolution) and treat it as prior art, not a format contract. The review read exact artifact notes/2026-08-28-disk-session-ingestion.md@3b086547b200a330ea3af2f764dc548856df4ffe and compared it with the current receiver, inbox, canonical-source rules, architecture, and implementation spec.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:2be1f002aef73a304c53749625cd6662c0151b3e","head":"3b086547b200a330ea3af2f764dc548856df4ffe","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:2a32641f7470cbdd8e266aae323ebcf61b6c00d0\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:2a32641f7470cbdd8e266aae323ebcf61b6c00d0","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}